<section class="section section-rule" id="practice">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div class="eyebrow"><span class="num">01</span>Practice</div>
      <div>
        <div class="section-kicker">
          ISO 19650 consultancy &middot; Common Data Environment implementation &middot; Golden Thread compliance
        </div>
        <h2 class="section-title">
          A small practice for a discipline that <em>rewards depth, not breadth.</em>
        </h2>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="practice-grid">
      <aside class="practice-aside">
        <div class="etymology">
          <div class="word">sylfaen</div>
          <div class="pron">[ˈsəlvain] &middot; Welsh, n.</div>
          <p class="def">
            <span class="pos">noun.</span>
            Foundation. The base upon which a structure stands; that without
            which everything else fails quietly, then loudly.
          </p>
        </div>
        <figure style="margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;">
          <div class="is-portrait" style="border: 1px solid var(--rule); overflow: hidden; background: #1a1612;">
            <img
              src="/assets/divider-desk.jpg"
              alt="A pencil sketch of a building elevation on a wooden desk"
              style="width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; object-position: 20% 80%; display: block; filter: saturate(0.75) contrast(1.05) brightness(0.92);"
            />
          </div>
          <figcaption style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--slate);">
            <span>Pl. II &middot; At the desk</span>
            <span>Where engagements begin</span>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </aside>

      <div class="practice-body">
        <p class="lead">
          Sylfaen Advisory exists because information management on UK
          construction projects is, with regrettable consistency, an
          afterthought &mdash; outsourced to template libraries, retrofitted into
          CDE platforms purchased for other reasons, and audited only when
          something has already gone wrong.
        </p>
        <p>
          We work in the opposite direction. ISO 19650 is not a wrapper we
          apply at the end of a project; it is the foundation we begin from.
          Our engagements are deliberately compact &mdash; diagnostics measured
          in weeks, implementations measured in months &mdash; because depth of
          expertise is what produces results, not breadth of staffing.
        </p>
        <p>
          The practice serves three audiences without diluting any of them:
          Tier 1 contractors needing assured information pipelines, asset
          owners building Golden Thread compliance, and mid-size
          consultancies retaining fractional information management.
        </p>

        <div class="practice-stats">
          <div class="practice-stat">
            <div class="v">15<span class="suffix">+ yrs</span></div>
            <div class="k">CDE delivery experience across health, infrastructure and housebuilding</div>
          </div>
          <div class="practice-stat">
            <div class="v">6</div>
            <div class="k">Major platforms covered &mdash; Asite, Autodesk Docs, Dalux, ProjectWise, Viewpoint, BCDE</div>
          </div>
          <div class="practice-stat">
            <div class="v">14<span class="suffix">d</span></div>
            <div class="k">Standard Health Check turnaround, from kick-off to remediation roadmap</div>
          </div>
          <div class="practice-stat">
            <div class="v">6</div>
            <div class="k">Sectors served &mdash; infrastructure, health, education, nuclear, defence, housebuilding</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
